SUMMARY:Create a poppy suncatcher
DESCRIPTION:Pop into Anzac Square Memorial Galleries during the spring scho
 ol holidays to create your own poppy suncatcher. Let's get crafty! Suitabl
 e for all ages\, this free family-friendly craft activity is available bet
 ween 10 am – 4pm daily from 20 September to 4 October (closed Saturdays)
 . Bookings are not required\, simply visit the craft table in our Post Wor
 ld War II Gallery. Facilitated by our knowledgeable team\, this activity w
 ill explore the special connection between poppies and Australia’s milit
 ary past. A resilient flower\, the red poppy was amongst the first to retu
 rn to bloom in the fields of France and Belgium after World War I\, emergi
 ng as a symbol of remembrance for the Allied soldiers who fell in battle. 
 Once you've created your poppy suncatcher\, stay to explore the Memorial G
 alleries\, embarking on an interactive journey from World War I to today\,
  before taking time to reflect on the remarkable stories of bravery and sa
 crifice in the tranquil parklands.
